## tender-db-verify.timer — fires the standing gate once per snapshot (task #28).
##
## WHY A FIXED TIME IS SAFE HERE, despite the daily pipeline having no fixed end.
## The daily fires 09:35 Europe/Berlin and the fold's duration varies by hours, so
## this cannot be scheduled "after the snapshot" by clock arithmetic. It does not
## need to be: the gate carries FAIL_ON_REPEAT=1, so if it fires before a new
## snapshot exists it sees the same input identity as last run and REFUSES rather
## than re-verifying yesterday's photograph and reporting a fresh green.
##
## That makes a too-early firing self-correcting rather than dangerous, which is
## what lets the schedule be simple. The failure it converts is the important one:
## a green reported for a cycle that produced nothing.
##
## 04:00 is ~18h after the 09:35 tick — comfortably past a long fold, and in the
## quietest part of the day, which the bounded-deferral interlock then only has to
## improve on rather than rescue.

[Unit]
Description=Daily structural verification of the canonical layer

[Timer]
OnCalendar=*-*-* 04:00:00
## A missed run (box down, deploy) still verifies rather than silently skipping a
## day. The gate's own repeat detection makes a late run harmless: if the snapshot
## has not moved it refuses, and if it has, verifying it is exactly the point.
Persistent=true
## Nothing else contends for 04:00, but a fixed instant across units is a habit
## worth not forming.
RandomizedDelaySec=300

[Install]
WantedBy=timers.target
